# A giver's work (Docs/Design/83-dialogue-trees.md, Phase 2): what work there is, a job's details (where, what, the pay,
# the time it has, the risks), taking it on or not; and, coming back, how it stands and giving it back (free, with no
# penalty: the user's answer). Entered from a keeper's "Any work going?", the wheel's "Ask for work" and "Ask about:
# ..." (job, bound), a faction official's board (a mission, bound), and "About the work I took on" (mine).
#
# The giver's lines are talk concepts (dlg.work.<node>): a trade's, a dialect's or a resident's own rule outranks
# these. The bound job's facts are #job.x# (topic.job_x): title, reward, directions, due, risk, progress, state (open,
# taken, done, expired, gone), allowed and why (yes only when the server would let this wolf take it now), source
# (contract or mission). A tree can do nothing the wheel couldn't: take, decline and give_back are the game's own.

tree work
entry work list
entry job job
entry mine mine

node list
say #work_offer# | This is what's going. | Work? Aye, some.
say[here.work=0 priority=2] #work_none# | #work_none# Ask again tomorrow.
each job in here.work max 4
choice What about this one: #job.title# (#job.reward#p)? [topic.job_allowed=yes] locked "#job.why#" -> job
choice I wanted to ask about the work I took on. [here.mine>0] -> mine
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node job
say #job.directions#
say[topic.job_state=taken|done|expired|gone priority=5] #job.why#
mood keen
choice I'll take it on. [topic.job_allowed=yes] locked "#job.why#" -> do take job.id ; then taken ; refused refused
choice What does it pay, and by when? [topic.job_state=open] -> terms
choice Is there any danger in it? [topic.job_state=open] -> risk
choice Not for me, thanks. -> do decline ; then declined

node terms
say #job.reward# pennies when it's done. It wants doing #job.due#. | It pays #job.reward# pennies, #job.due#.
say[topic.job_reward=0 priority=2] There's no pay in it, mind. It wants doing #job.due#.
choice I'll take it on. [topic.job_allowed=yes] locked "#job.why#" -> do take job.id ; then taken ; refused refused
choice Is there any danger in it? -> risk
choice Tell me again what it is. -> job
choice Not for me, thanks. -> do decline ; then declined

node risk
say #job.risk#
choice I'll take it on. [topic.job_allowed=yes] locked "#job.why#" -> do take job.id ; then taken ; refused refused
choice What does it pay, and by when? -> terms
choice Not for me, thanks. -> do decline ; then declined

node taken
say #work_taken# It's marked on your map. | #work_taken#
mood pleased
choice What else is there? [topic.job_source=contract] -> list
choice What else is there? [topic.job_source=mission] -> do open missions
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node declined
say #work_declined#
choice What else is there? [topic.job_source=contract] -> list
choice What else is there? [topic.job_source=mission] -> do open missions
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node refused
say #topic.why# | Not so fast. #topic.why#
choice What else is there? [topic.job_source=contract] -> list
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node mine
say Which of them? | What about it? | Go on, then.
say[here.mine=0 priority=2] You've nothing of mine in hand.
each job in here.mine max 4
choice About this one: #job.title#. -> progress
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node progress
say #job.progress#
choice Remind me what it is. -> again
choice I can't do it after all. -> do give_back job.id ; then given ; refused refused
choice I'll get on with it. -> bye

node again
say #job.directions#
choice I can't do it after all. -> do give_back job.id ; then given ; refused refused
choice I'll get on with it. -> bye

node given
say #work_back#
mood calm
choice What else is there? [topic.job_source=contract] -> list
choice Goodbye for now. -> bye

node bye
say #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
end
